pport now lists `generated/hello-world.mjs` as a stale dependency. That result stays historical evidence and the recorded justification for the correction; it must not be retargeted to the new bytes. The constructor says its own post-edit run passed, but that is an attributed report, not admitted evidence. So there is currently no admitted observation of the corrected CLI, and the behavior and revision obligations both lack current verifier execution. The construction work is complete and sufficient for its bounded purpose. It should be reused, not rerun. Under the steel-thread approach, the next consequential uncertainty is whether the corrected runnable path actually works when measured. This needs a fresh C2 run of both fixed commands against the current bytes, tied to the construction result so the chain from baseline failure through correction to current evidence is explicit. `specification/project-conformance.md`, `design/implementation-design.md`, `design/test-design.md` and `test-execution-plan.json` are still absent, so their four obligations remain open. The final independent UAT still has to assess everything once these exist. All seven obligations remain open.\",\"contributions\":[{\"graphFunctionRef\":\"graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/testing@5\",\"contribution\":\"Re-measure the corrected current CLI (sha256:fe8f4080…) produced by construction result e897db22, using the fixed command plan:\\n1. `node generated/hello-world.mjs`\\n2. `node --test test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs`\\n\\nFor each command, record the real executable, args, cwd, environment, exit status, signal, stdout, stderr, and the resulting test/pass/fail counts, exactly as observed, including any nonzero exit or failure. Do not edit any file. Baseline result 6514754a stays historical evidence about the earlier bytes; do not merge it with or overwrite it by the new observation.\",\"reason\":\"Behavior requires admitted current evidence on the corrected subject: exit 0, stdout exactly `Hello, world!\\\\n`, at least two real passing tests and zero failures. Revision requires a consequential same-lineage correction whose effect is actually observed. The only admitted execution evidence (6514754a) is stale for current-behavior claims, and the constructor's self-check is not recorded evidence. Selecting the construction result as the testing subject keeps the chain from failure through correction to re-measurement explicit.\",\"supportRefs\":[\"obligation://default-library-witness/behavior@5\",\"obligation://default-library-witness/revision@5\",\"obligation://default-library-witness/complete-original@5\"],\"evidenceRefs\":[\"task://default-library-witness/s6-original@5\",\"worksite-context-observation://abiogenesis/08dd3a898b57a4f0437501a4ad2f9345963e3371c4b5cb84aaef6ea4161fa827\",\"result://abiogenesis/6514754aa979c64827c955c618e60ece86ef79274b734c3844f2a13243a95d5c\",\"result://abiogenesis/e897db2208fad8afe99c5a184cddd24cb96421de5bb7df496a193774769cc41c\"],\"dependsOn\":[]},{\"graphFunctionRef\":\"graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/specification@5\",\"contribution\":\"Write `specification/project-conformance.md` for a minimal CLI Hello World software-build traversal. It must state:\\n- the Intent;\\n- the Product boundary: a Node CLI with no package or network dependency;\\n- source-grounded requirements;\\n- completion criteria.\\n\\nThe source surface is `generated/hello-world.mjs`. The execution proof runs the CLI and observes stdout of exactly `Hello, world!\\\\n` with exit 0. Completion also requires both supplied component and UAT tests to execute the real CLI, with at least two passes and zero failures, backed by truthful admitted execution evidence rather than a prewritten report. Write no source, tests, package files or execution plans.\",\"reason\":\"The file is absent, and the conformance obligation needs fresh substantive content grounded in the original conformance_project stage. The content does not depend on the CLI bytes. It is the authority for the implementation design.\",\"supportRefs\":[\"obligation://default-library-witness/conformance@5\",\"obligation://default-library-witness/complete-original@5\"],\"evidenceRefs\":[\"task://default-library-witness/s6-original@5\",\"worksite-context-observation://abiogenesis/08dd3a898b57a4f0437501a4ad2f9345963e3371c4b5cb84aaef6ea4161fa827\"],\"dependsOn\":[]},{\"graphFunctionRef\":\"graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/design@5\",\"contribution\":\"Write three files:\\n1. `design/implementation-design.md`: uses the conformance artifact as authority. Defines the minimal Node CLI at `generated/hello-world.mjs`, which prints exactly `Hello, world!` followed by one newline, and describes the actual corrected source surface. Names the component and UAT test source surfaces (`test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs`, `test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs`) that execute the CLI and assert stdout.\\n2. `design/test-design.md`: specifies component and UAT validation. Both tests spawn `node generated/hello-world.mjs` from the project root and assert status 0 and stdout of exactly `Hello, world!\\\\n`.\\n3. `test-execution-plan.json`: command `node`; args `[\\\"--test\\\",\\\"test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs\\\",\\\"test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs\\\"]`; `expectedTestPassCount` of at least 2; `expectedStdoutMatch` with stable zero-failure evidence such as `fail 0` and no exact pass-count fragment; `assertedReturnValue` of `Hello, world!`.\\n\\nThe plan must agree with the fixed commands but does not control execution.\",\"reason\":\"All three files are absent. Each obligation needs fresh content that is faithful to the original source and to the conformance predecessor. The implementation design should describe the corrected current CLI surface that construction has already produced.\",\"supportRefs\":[\"obligation://default-library-witness/implementation-design@5\",\"obligation://default-library-witness/test-design@5\",\"obligation://default-library-witness/execution-plan@5\",\"obligation://default-library-witness/complete-original@5\"],\"evidenceRefs\":[\"task://default-library-witness/s6-original@5\",\"worksite-context-observation://abiogenesis/08dd3a898b57a4f0437501a4ad2f9345963e3371c4b5cb84aaef6ea4161fa827\",\"result://abiogenesis/e897db2208fad8afe99c5a184cddd24cb96421de5bb7df496a193774769cc41c\"],\"dependsOn\":[\"graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/specification@5\"]},{\"graphFunctionRef\":\"graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/uat@5\",\"contribution\":\"Independent, read-only assessment against the original source, the oracle rubric and the witness contract. It covers:\\n- the authored conformance, implementation design, test design and execution-plan content, and how each corresponds to the source and to its predecessor;\\n- whether the supplied component and UAT tests are adequate verifiers of the real CLI;\\n- whether the plan agrees with the fixed commands and original expectations;\\n- the causal chain from the historical baseline failure (6514754a) through the bounded correction (e897db22);\\n- current admitted command evidence on the corrected CLI: exit 0, exact stdout, at least two passes, zero failures.\\n\\nUnmet and indeterminate criteria must be kept, not dropped.\",\"reason\":\"Parent completion requires a semantic assessment of exact current evidence by an actor distinct from the authors and the measurement producer. It can only run once the authored assets and fresh current-subject evidence exist.\",\"supportRefs\":[\"obligation://default-library-witness/complete-original@5\",\"obligation://default-library-witness/conformance@5\",\"obligation://default-library-witness/implementation-design@5\",\"obligation://default-library-witness/test-design@5\",\"obligation://default-library-witness/execution-plan@5\",\"obligation://default-library-witness/behavior@5\",\"obligation://default-library-witness/revision@5\"],\"evidenceRefs\":[\"task://default-library-witness/s6-original@5\",\"result://abiogenesis/6514754aa979c64827c955c618e60ece86ef79274b734c3844f2a13243a95d5c\",\"result://abiogenesis/e897db2208fad8afe99c5a184cddd24cb96421de5bb7df496a193774769cc41c\"],\"dependsOn\":[\"graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/specification@5\",\"graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/design@5\",\"graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/testing@5\"]}],\"gaps\":[],\"nextGraphFunctionRef\":\"graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/testing@5\",\"nextReason\":\"Construction (e897db22) changed the CLI bytes, so the only admitted execution evidence (6514754a) is stale for current behavior. The constructor's passing self-check is not admitted evidence. Re-measuring the corrected subject now, with the fixed commands, is the cheapest step that settles the main open question: does the corrected steel thread actually run and pass? It also supplies the verifier-execution role that behavior and revision both require. The construction native-work result is selected as the testing subject so the measurement is explicitly tied to the correction that follows the historical baseline failure.\",\"nextEvidenceRefs\":[\"task://default-library-witness/s6-original@5\",\"worksite-context-observation://abiogenesis/08dd3a898b57a4f0437501a4ad2f9345963e3371c4b5cb84aaef6ea4161fa827\",\"result://abiogenesis/6514754aa979c64827c955c618e60ece86ef79274b734c3844f2a13243a95d5c\",\"result://abiogenesis/e897db2208fad8afe99c5a184cddd24cb96421de5bb7df496a193774769cc41c\"],\"subjectEvidenceRef\":\"result://abiogenesis/e897db2208fad8afe99c5a184cddd24cb96421de5bb7df496a193774769cc41c\",\"revisionReason\":\"The prior judgment (3967846e) chose construction next. It ran as result e897db22 and made the bounded fix to `generated/hello-world.mjs` only (now sha256:fe8f4080…); the worksite observation 08dd3a89 confirms protected files are unchanged. That work is complete and sufficient, so I removed construction from the current mapping and cite i